      "## What Is Dollar-Cost Averaging?",
      "Dollar-cost averaging is an investing strategy where you invest a predetermined amount of money at regular intervals, regardless of short-term market movements. You don't stop investing simply because the market is down. You don't necessarily increase your contribution because the market is up. You follow your predetermined plan. The result is that you purchase investments at different prices over time.",
      "## A Simple $100 Example",
      "Let's say you decide to invest $100 every month into an investment. Here's a simplified example:",
      "| Month | Investment Price | Amount Invested | Units Purchased |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| January | $10 | $100 | 10.00 |\n| February | $8 | $100 | 12.50 |\n| March | $12 | $100 | 8.33 |\n| April | $10 | $100 | 10.00 |\n| **Total** | | **$400** | **40.83** |",
      "Your average price per unit is approximately: $400 ÷ 40.83 = $9.80",
