      "## Why Does DCA Appeal to Beginners?",
      "For many new investors, the biggest advantage isn't necessarily mathematical. It's psychological. Investing a large amount all at once can be intimidating. Imagine you have $10,000 sitting in cash. You invest all of it today. Tomorrow, the market falls 10%. Your investment could now be worth approximately $9,000. Even though nothing fundamentally changed about your long-term goal, seeing that immediate decline can cause anxiety. A DCA approach might instead spread those contributions over time. That doesn't eliminate investment risk, but it can make the process feel more manageable for some investors.",
      "## DCA Doesn't Mean You Avoid Market Declines",
