      "The goal isn't to constantly change your strategy. It's to establish a system you can follow.",
      "## What Happens When Your Income Increases?",
      "This is where DCA becomes even more powerful. Suppose you start with $100/month. Then you receive a raise. You increase your contribution to $150/month. Later, $200/month. Then $300/month. You're essentially allowing your investment strategy to grow alongside your income. You don't have to start big. You can grow into a bigger investor.",
      "## The Biggest Advantage of DCA May Be Discipline",
      "There's an interesting lesson here. The biggest benefit of dollar-cost averaging may not be that it produces a magical mathematical advantage. It doesn't. The real advantage for many people is that it creates a repeatable behavior. You decide how much you're going to invest. You establish a schedule. You automate it where appropriate. You continue learning. You track your progress. And you give your investments time. That's a powerful combination.",
